---
import { COMPETITORS, COMPETITORS_CHECKED, PRICING, SITE, TRIAL } from '../consts';

/**
 * The named comparison, built from `COMPETITORS` in src/consts.ts.
 *
 * It exists as a component rather than as a table typed into the article so
 * that **no price is ever written into prose**. The article discusses these
 * apps in words — "a subscription", "one unlock", "a one-time purchase" — and
 * every figure on the page comes from here, which comes from the constants,
 * which record where each was read and when. One number, one home.
 *
 * Rows with no price are not a gap. They are two companies whose figures we
 * could not confirm first-hand on the date below, and saying so is more useful
 * to a reader than a number we would not stand behind.
 */
---

<div class="rivals">
  <!-- The scroll lives on a labelled, focusable region rather than on the
       table. A pane that scrolls but cannot be reached by keyboard is a pane
       some readers simply cannot see the last column of. -->
  <div
    class="rivals__scroll"
    role="region"
    aria-label="What each budgeting app costs"
    tabindex="0"
  >
    <table>
      <caption>
        What each one costs, checked against first-party sources on{' '}
        <time datetime={COMPETITORS_CHECKED.on}>
          {COMPETITORS_CHECKED.display}</time
        >. <span class="rivals__hint">Scrolls sideways.</span>
      </caption>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">App</th>
        <th scope="col">Price</th>
        <th scope="col">How it is charged</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="rivals__ours">
        <th scope="row">{SITE.name}</th>
        <td>{PRICING.full}</td>
        <td>
          {PRICING.note}. {TRIAL.days}-day trial. <em>Ours — see below.</em>
        </td>
      </tr>
      {
        COMPETITORS.map((rival) => (
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">
              <a href={rival.url}>{rival.name}</a>
            </th>
            <td>{rival.price ?? <span class="rivals__none">Not printed</span>}</td>
            <td>{rival.priceNote}</td>
          </tr>
        ))
      }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="small muted">
    Two rows carry no figure. Their prices could not be confirmed from a
    first-party source on the date above — one publishes only a promotional
    price, the other publishes none — and a number we cannot stand behind is
    worse than an admission. Follow the links and check for yourself; that is
    what they are there for.
  </p>
</div>

<style>
  .rivals {
    margin: var(--space-xl) 0 var(--space-2xl);
  }

  /* Three columns of prose do not fit a phone; let the table scroll inside
     itself rather than push the page sideways. */
  .rivals__scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .rivals__scroll:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--focus);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .rivals table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
  }

  /* Only say "scrolls sideways" when it does. */
  .rivals__hint {
    display: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 46rem) {
    .rivals__hint {
      display: inline;
    }
  }

  .rivals caption {
    text-align: left;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-s);
  }

  .rivals td,
  .rivals th {
    min-width: 8rem;
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  .rivals td:last-child {
    min-width: 18rem;
    white-space: normal;
  }

  .rivals__ours th,
  .rivals__ours td {
    color: var(--text-accent);
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .rivals__ours em {
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .rivals__none {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
